  "precedence_rules": [
    "The authoritative path/locator named here wins over any other statement in any bound payload.",
    "A derived mirror never creates a requirement; it only restates one.",
    "CANDIDATE_EXECUTION_SEAL.json is authoritative ONLY for status_at_audit_submission; the detached attestation is the sole authority for post-audit acceptance state.",
    "PAYLOAD_HASHES.json must carry no status field.",
    "Deprecated literals must not appear as a requirement in any bound payload, in code or in prose.",
    "An EXTERNAL: prefix marks an authoritative source that lies outside the candidate namespace and is verified by the runner rather than by the package gate."
  ],
  "purpose": "One enumerated normative source per load-bearing concept. The gate does not check a hand-written mirror list; it sweeps the bound closure for value-shaped tokens and requires every discovered token to be attributed to a concept and found only at that concept's authoritative path or a declared mirror.",
